From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] luma: tiling layouts follow the monitor and the monitor setup

Tiling Shell stored one layout per workspace per monitor position, so when
monitors reconnected in another order, one was unplugged, or the laptop
moved between desks, layouts landed on the wrong screens. Layouts chosen
by the person are now remembered for each combination of connected
monitors and for each physical monitor (maker, model and serial). When the
monitors change the setup's own layouts come back, and a setup never seen
before gives each monitor its most recent layouts. The memory lives in
~/.local/share/luma/tiling-layout-memory.json.

